Third-party material bundled in the ledger apps.

Both apps ship the first three items — ledger 1.0 from frontend/, ledger 2.0
from web/. The fourth ships in ledger 2.0 only. There is no in-app credits
screen; this file is the attribution.

Geist and Geist Mono
  Copyright 2024 The Geist Project Authors
  (https://github.com/vercel/geist-font)
  SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1 (http://scripts.sil.org/OFL)

  Shipped as the .woff2 files in each built bundle, via the npm packages
  @fontsource-variable/geist and @fontsource-variable/geist-mono, which are
  imported in frontend/src/main.tsx and web/src/main.tsx. Each of those packages
  ships the full licence text in its own LICENSE file, under the node_modules of
  whichever app you are looking at — frontend/ and web/ each install both.

Pixelarticons
  Copyright (c) 2019 Gerrit Halfmann
  (https://github.com/halfmage/pixelarticons)
  MIT License

  Both apps take their icon set from here. The SVG path data is
  generated into src/components/ui/pixelIcons.ts by
  scripts/generate-pixel-icons.mjs, from pixelarticons 2.2.0. The npm package
  is a devDependency, so what ships is the path data rather than the package.

dither-kit 0.1.0
  https://www.tripwire.sh/dither-kit

  Vendored source under src/components/dither-kit/ in both apps, installed with
  `shadcn add https://tripwire.sh/r/bar-chart.json` and then modified in place
  (the changes are listed in that directory's README.md). The registry payload
  itself ships no licence file, but dither-kit is built on EvilCharts
  (https://github.com/legions-developer/evilcharts), which is MIT-licensed:
  Copyright (c) 2026 Gurbinder. The MIT terms (use, modification and
  redistribution permitted with this notice) cover the vendored code.

sql.js (ledger 2.0 only)
  Copyright (c) 2017 sql.js authors
  MIT License

  Shipped as the sql-wasm .wasm file in web/'s bundle: it is the SQLite engine
  the browser client runs its local database on. sql.js is SQLite compiled to
  WebAssembly; SQLite itself is public domain.

The JavaScript bundles also link the npm libraries declared in
frontend/package.json and web/package.json. React and React DOM, TanStack Query
and TanStack Table, Tailwind CSS, Motion, clsx and tailwind-merge are all MIT
licensed; d3-scale and d3-shape are ISC.
